# Do not regress shipped features

Do not delete, hide, or bypass a behavior that already shipped (store review login, session/logout, account linking, phone/email field split, and anything in README smoke or store docs) unless this conversation explicitly says to remove it.

If the current prompt is about recaptcha, linking, search, or another area, leave unrelated shipped auth paths unchanged. Do not "simplify" login while fixing something else.

# Google Play review login (protected)

Reviewers type `google-review@gocha.ai` and a password. OTP is skipped. This must work on Sign in and on Create your account, on https://app.gocha.ai/ and on native.

- Password field: `shouldShowReviewPasswordField` in `mobile/gocha-app/src/auth/reviewLogin.ts`. Do not gate it on `mode === 'signup'` or `!isSignUp`.
- API: `POST /api/auth/review/login` plus Infisical `GOCHA_REVIEW_LOGIN_EMAIL` / `GOCHA_REVIEW_LOGIN_PASSWORD`.
- Tests: `mobile/gocha-app/__tests__/reviewLoginField.test.ts` and `app_gocha/tests/Feature/AuthReviewLoginTest.php`. Do not delete or weaken them to land other work.
- Smoke after any EmailScreen or auth-meta change: type `google-review@gocha.ai` on Create account and on Sign in; the Password field must appear without tapping anything else.

If a task would make that field disappear, stop and keep the field.
